  --id-at-source: record # <dfn class="text-muted"><p class="mb-2">optional, string filter</p></dfn> <p class="mb-2">The identifier of the subscription in the <a href="omnichannel_subscriptions#omnichannel_subscriptions_source" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline"><code class="bg-gray-100 text-gray-800 font-medium border border-gray-300 rounded px-1.5 py-0.5 mx-1 text-sm font-mono whitespace-nowrap">source</code></a>. For Apple App Store, this is the initial purchase <strong class="font-semibold">Transaction ID</strong>; for Google Play Store this is the <strong class="font-semibold">Order ID</strong>. <strong class="font-semibold">Supported operators :</strong> is, is_not, starts_with, in, not_in</p> <p class="mb-2"><strong class="font-semibold">Example →</strong> <em class="italic">id_at_source[is] = &quot;2000000123456789&quot;</em></p> (e.g. 2000001162945130)
